# The build context is the workspace root, because planner-server depends on
# planner-core by path and a narrower context cannot see it. That makes this
# file load-bearing before the first build rather than after: `target/` alone
# is gigabytes, and it is uploaded before any instruction runs.
#
# The Containerfile then copies an explicit list rather than the whole context,
# so this only has to stop the large and the secret.
target/
.git/
.flatpak-build/
dist/

# These reach the container through the environment, never through a layer,
# where they would survive in the image whatever the running process does.
server/.env
packaging/.env
